# Contributing to <%= projectName %>

Thank you for considering contributing to **<%= projectName %>**.

## Getting Started

1. Fork the repository
2. Create a task branch: `git checkout -b task/#NNN-short-description`
3. Make your changes following the guidelines below
4. Run the quality gate: `<%= testCommand %>`
5. Commit with the [conventional format](#commit-format)
6. Open a Pull Request

## Branch Naming

```
task/#NNN-short-description
```

Where `#NNN` is the GitHub issue number. No direct commits to `main`.

## Commit Format

```
type(scope): summary

- Detail of what changed
- Detail of what changed
```

**Types:** `feat`, `fix`, `refactor`, `test`, `docs`, `chore`, `ci`

## Code Standards

See `AGENTS.md` for the full coding standards, invariants, and testing policy.

Key rules:
- The frozen delivery candidate must pass the quality gate; checkpoint commits retain staged safety checks<% if (language === 'typescript') { %>
- No `any` types — use proper type annotations<% } %><% if (language === 'rust') { %>
- No `.unwrap()` — use proper error handling<% } %>
- No orphan TODOs — every `TODO` must reference a task ID (`TODO(#NNN)`)
- Tests required for new functionality

## Quality Gate

```bash
<%= testCommand %>
```

<% if (lintCommand) { %>**Lint:** `<%= lintCommand %>`
<% } %><% if (formatCommand) { %>**Format:** `<%= formatCommand %>`
<% } %>
**Adding a project-local check:** create `scripts/check-all.local.json` with a `checks` array of
`{ name, cmd, tier }` entries (plain JSON, not a script) — `scripts/check-all.mjs` reads it at
runtime and runs each one at its declared tier (`L1`/`L2`/`L3`/`L4`), labeled `[local] <name>` in
the summary. This file is never generated by `arbiter update`, so it is never overwritten or
withheld — it is the place for checks specific to this project, instead of hand-editing the gate
spine itself.

## Pull Requests

- Fill out the PR template completely
- Link the related issue
- Ensure the gate passes in CI
- Request review from a code owner

## Questions?

Open a [discussion](https://github.com/<%= githubOwner %>/<%= githubRepo %>/discussions) or reach out to the maintainers.
